{
  "_comment": "BugPilot 0.1.6 plan §8.10, the storage JSON contract, frozen as test data in Batch 1 (plan §14.2, step 9). No product code reads it. tests/test_storage_identity.py checks that it matches the plan's tables exactly; Batch 2's tests/test_storage_contract.py and extension/test/storageContract.test.ts will test against it. Machine-readable: `entries` restates each row of `keys` (same order, `row` counts from 1) as typed fields; tests/test_storage_identity.py anchors every field to its prose row, so the two cannot drift apart.",
  "status": "APPROVED IN PART (US-D26, by the owner, 2026-10-16): plan §8.10's contract semantics and the typed `entries` are frozen. Not approved: the `open_choices` below, and every row that depends on a decision still to be made or carried out: US-D4 (`below_git_toplevel`), US-D16 (removing `ai_artifacts_ignored*`), US-D18 (`--feedback-file`), US-D25 (`run.json`), and US-D3's deprecated-variable handling, which is Batch 2 work (`legacy_config_dir_variable`)",
  "id_pattern": "^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9._-]{0,23}-[0-9a-f]{16}$",
  "kinds": [
    {
      "kind": "abs",
      "definition": "an absolute path in the platform's own separators. No trailing separator, never `~`; the canonical form `storage` computed.",
      "example": "`C:\\Users\\you\\.bugpilot\\repositories\\app-0123456789abcdef\\work\\JR-12345`; `/home/you/.bugpilot/repositories/app-0123456789abcdef/work/JR-12345`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "ns",
      "definition": "relative to the repository namespace folder. `/` on every OS; no leading `./`; never `..`.",
      "example": "`work/JR-12345/task.md`, `memory/JR-12345.md`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "display",
      "definition": "the display form of §8.2: `~/.bugpilot/…` or `BUGPILOT_HOME/…`, with `/`. Never the user's own folder name.",
      "example": "`~/.bugpilot/repositories/app-0123456789abcdef/work/JR-12345/task.md`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "posix-abs",
      "definition": "`abs` written with `/`. Used only inside prompt and handoff text.",
      "example": "`C:/Users/you/.bugpilot/repositories/app-0123456789abcdef/work/JR-12345/task.md`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "id",
      "definition": "a repository ID matching `^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9._-]{0,23}-[0-9a-f]{16}$`",
      "example": "`app-0123456789abcdef`"
    }
  ],
